.TH ASTERCTL-PUBLISH 1 "2026-09-28" "Aster" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
asterctl-publish \- publish an Event to Aster
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY asterctl
.RI [ GLOBAL-OPTIONS ]
.B publish
.BI \-\-topic " TOPIC"
.BI \-\-scope " SCOPE"
.BI \-\-operation\-key " KEY|auto"
.RI [ PUBLISH-OPTIONS ]
.RI [ MSG ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B asterctl publish
publishes an Event to the Aster system through a running Aster agent.
.PP
If
.I MSG
is supplied, use it as the payload.
Otherwise, read the payload from standard input until EOF.
When standard input is a terminal, instructions are printed to stderr before
reading. Press Ctrl-D on an empty line to send, or Ctrl-C to cancel.
No input instructions are printed for a pipe, an explicit MSG, or a tombstone.
.PP
The agent assigns the Event ID, publisher identity, and sequence numbers.
.PP
The payload may contain text, JSON, or arbitrary binary data.
The agent limits the complete publication request to 1 MiB.
.PP
Exactly one of
.B \-\-token
or
.B \-\-token\-file
is required; see
.BR asterctl (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-topic " TOPIC"
Required. Select the Event topic, for example chat.events.
.IP
Must contain 1\(en128 ASCII characters: letters, digits, periods,
underscores, or hyphens.
.IP
The target node must be authorized to publish to this topic
within the selected scope.
.TP
.BI \-\-scope " SCOPE"
Required. Select the propagation and authorization scope.
.IP
Must contain 1\(en128 ASCII characters. Permitted characters are letters,
digits, periods, underscores, hyphens, and slashes separating path segments.
.IP
Leading or trailing slashes, empty segments, and segments consisting of
"." or ".." are not allowed.
.IP
Example: mission-1/team/alpha_2.
.TP
.BI \-\-priority " PRIORITY"
Set the Event priority for scheduling and storage policy.
.IP
Values, from lowest to highest: routine, priority, immediate, flash.
.IP
Default: routine.
.TP
.BI \-\-logical\-key " KEY"
Associate the Event with a UTF-8 text key.
.IP
Events may share a logical key. Publishing another Event with the same key
does not replace earlier Events.
.IP
Maximum: 4096 bytes. Default: empty.
.TP
.BI \-\-predecessor " ID"
Declare a causal dependency on another Event on the target node.
The predecessor may belong to another topic.
.IP
ID is a Base64-encoded 32-byte Event ID.
.IP
Default: none.
.TP
.BI \-\-ttl\-ms " MILLISECONDS"
Set the Event lifetime in milliseconds.
.IP
Must be a positive unsigned 64-bit integer. Zero is invalid.
The lifetime does not restart when the Event is forwarded.
.IP
After expiry, the Event is withheld from queries, delivery, and forwarding.
Storage maintenance subsequently removes its content.
.IP
Default: no expiry.
.TP
.B \-\-tombstone
Publish an Event marked as a tombstone.
.IP
Requires an empty payload and cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-ttl\-ms .
.IP
Default: false.
.TP
.BI \-\-operation\-key " KEY|auto"
Use a UTF-8 key of 1\(en256 bytes, or
.B auto
to generate a new key.
.IP
For retries, use the actual key from the previous attempt and the same
payload and publication parameters.
.SH OUTPUT
Prints the publication receipt to stdout.
With \-\-json, the receipt also includes
.BR operation_key .
.PP
Generated operation keys are also printed to stderr before sending the request.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Publication succeeded, including an idempotent retry.
.TP
.B 1
Command failed or the operation's outcome is unknown.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid or missing arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
Publish text:
.PP
.nf
.RS
asterctl \-\-token\-file ./client.token publish \e
    \-\-topic chat.events \e
    \-\-scope mission/team/alpha \e
    \-\-operation\-key auto \e
    "Hello, Aster!"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Publish a file:
.PP
.nf
.RS
cat "file.json" | asterctl \-\-token\-file ./client.token publish \e
    \-\-topic chat.events \e
    \-\-scope mission/team/alpha \e
    \-\-operation\-key file-001
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR asterctl (1)
